[[!meta title="Greeter storage"]]

# Introduction

Tails provides the user with the ability to store sensitive data encrypted in the Persistent Storage.
However, some bits need to be loaded *before* reaching the Greeter, to allow the user to effectively use the
Tails Greeter: language and keymap.

## Sensitivity

Locale-related issues are not without concern, as has been extensively discussed on [[!tails_ticket 5501]].

It's therefore important to make this opt-in.

# Design

## Storage

The data are stored in Tails FAT (XXX: clarify) partition. A dedicated directory is created, and each "item"
is a file inside that.
